abstract: >-
  Case studies that apply GIS methods to social science questions. The first
  case study, on food deserts, covers low-income, low-access (LILA) census
  tracts, the USDA Food Access Research Atlas and its 2026 update, and two
  Google Colab notebooks that map the published Atlas for any U.S. state and
  rebuild the analysis from open Census and OpenStreetMap data.
